---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import HealthBlock from '../components/HealthBlock.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Health"
  description="Every Carter French Bulls puppy comes vaccinated, dewormed, microchipped, and vet-checked. Here is what each item means."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-intro">
        <h1>What comes with every puppy</h1>
        <p>
          Six things come included with every puppy we place. This is not a marketing promise —
          it is a factual list of what we do before any puppy goes home.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="health-block-wrap">
        <HealthBlock showCta={true} showPrice={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-sand">
    <div class="container health-detail-grid">

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Vaccinated</h2>
        <p>
          Each puppy receives the appropriate vaccines for their age before going home.
          The vaccination record comes with your puppy so your vet can continue the schedule.
        </p>
        <p>
          Puppies under 16 weeks typically receive their first combination vaccines.
          Your vet will advise on the next boosters.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Dewormed</h2>
        <p>
          Puppies are dewormed on a regular schedule starting at two weeks of age.
          This is standard care for any well-raised puppy and is part of what we do before placement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Microchipped</h2>
        <p>
          Every puppy is microchipped before leaving us. This is a permanent form of identification that
          cannot fall off or wear out. Keep your contact information updated with the chip registry.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Health certificate</h2>
        <p>
          A health certificate from a licensed veterinarian is available on request.
          This document is often required for travel, especially if your puppy is flying.
          Ask us about timing when you reserve.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact#reserve" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top:8px">
          Ask for the health certificate
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Registration included</h2>
        <p>
          Registration varies by litter. We will discuss the specific registration for your puppy
          directly — every puppy's situation is a little different, and we want to give you
          accurate information rather than a blanket claim.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="health-detail-item">
        <h2>Veterinary exam</h2>
        <p>
          A licensed veterinarian examines each puppy before they go home.
          The exam date is recorded in each puppy's profile on this site.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container trust-note">
      <h2>How to protect yourself</h2>
      <div class="trust-box">
        <p>
          Puppy scams are real, and we take them seriously. Here is how to stay safe when buying
          any puppy from any source:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>We never ask for payment without a signed agreement first.</li>
          <li>We will never ask you to send money by gift card or wire transfer.</li>
          <li>If you see our photos used on another site with a different contact, that is fraud. Report it.</li>
          <li>Ask questions before sending any money. A reputable breeder will always answer them.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you have any doubts, call us. We would rather lose a sale than have someone get scammed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-intro {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .page-intro p {
    color: var(--color-stone);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .health-block-wrap {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .health-detail-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .health-detail-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
    }
  }

  .health-detail-item h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .health-detail-item p {
    color: var(--color-stone);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .trust-note {
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .trust-box {
    padding: 28px 32px;
    background: var(--color-butter);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .trust-box p {
    color: var(--color-stone);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .trust-box ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .trust-box li {
    color: var(--color-stone);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
</style>
